# Generated files are LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true gives a Windows checkout CRLF in the working
# tree while the generator writes LF. `git add` normalises both to LF, so the
# CI gate is correct either way -- but `git status` reports all 17 generated
# files as modified immediately after a fresh checkout and a regeneration that
# changed nothing.
#
# SC-003 is "contracts regenerate with an empty git diff", and a developer
# checking that by eye would see 17 modified files and conclude the contract
# had drifted. A gate that cries wolf is a gate people learn to skip, so the
# line endings are pinned rather than left to each machine's git config.
* text eol=lf
